kindSRT -- STORE-THEN-READ ACROSS THE += CALL-THROUGH, compiled once, fired twice,
jitted beside interpreted (Clay's close-out, 2026-09-25).

local   srL is an action LOCAL -- a frame slot on the jitted road. It is assigned by
        `=`, then +=, then read: 7 then 12.
field   srG is a define-block field, stored through at its baked address: 7 then 9.
empty   srE is a local NEVER assigned before its +=, so it is EMPTY and picks by the
        argument's kind. Interpreted: 2 on every fire. JITTED: 2 then 4 -- PINNED AS A
        MEASURED DIVERGENCE, NOT A CLAIM. It is not the call-through: a jitted action
        LOCAL keeps its value across fires where the interpreted road clears it on
        every invocation. With no += at all, `ctL = ctL + 1` reads 1 2 3 jitted and
        0 0 0 interpreted (measured 2026-09-25). A frame-model finding, reported.

THE ROW THAT FOUND SOMETHING: before the fix the jitted LOCAL read 2 on fire 1 where
the interpreted road read 7. A frame slot carries a value, never a kind; the jitted `=`
put the count in the slot but gave the local no kind, so the call-through saw an EMPTY
target and copied the argument in. The fix is gJitFrameAssigned: a scalar `=` into a
frame slot is recorded, and the op-fire flush stamps the kind (setCount/setNumber) for
those slots only. The EMPTY row is its other half -- a local no `=` has written must
stay empty, and stamping every slot would type it as a count.
